      "detail": "[exceptionflow_exit_coverage] The first exception-flow claim says the alarm icon changes to normal when the alarm condition is removed, but it does not state that the use case terminates, returns to a main-flow step, hands off, or reaches an explicit terminal state; the branch lacks a clear use-case outcome. (atomic grounding: candidate remains incomplete (Whether the alarm condition being removed before operator acknowledgment is explicitly supported.; Whether the alarm-handling use case exits automatically when the alarm condition is removed.; Whether no further operator acknowledgment is required after the alarm condition is removed.))",
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
